  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-MSSP3 (codename machuca), Android TV 11 (SDK 30), firmware RTT2.211214.001.1065, MediaTek.\nLive TV app: com.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter (already the live_tv_package in launcher config.xml).\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (the default, disabled by build-and-install.sh).\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mssp3/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mssp3/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- Default IME is already Gboard, so the Mi TV 4A missing-keyboard quirk doesn't apply.\n- Left alone on purpose: com.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter / tvinput* (HDMI + tuner), mitv.service,\ncom.mi.bluetooth, com.mediatek.hotkey.dispatcher, com.google.android.tv.remote.service.\n- Netflix and Prime Video come back at every reboot even when disabled. The cause is\ncom.mstar.netflixobserver: it is a PERSISTENT app with the system uid, so Android starts it at boot even\nwhen it is disabled, and it re-enables both (it even re-installed them after pm uninstall --user 0).\nDisabling it is not enough. This list only disables it, like everything else in this repo.\nBeyond what this repo does, and your own call: removing it for user 0 worked here across a reboot\npm uninstall --user 0 com.mstar.netflixobserver\nand is undone with\ncmd package install-existing com.mstar.netflixobserver   (the remote's Netflix button needs it)\n- Device admin is not supported on this firmware (no android.software.device_admin).\nXiaomi + Google telemetry",
